{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited","id":1040292,"title":"Justice Democracy's (very excited)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T16:53:21-08:00","id":1040292,"title":"Justice Democracy's (very excited)","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_Democrats\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Justice_Democrats_logo.svg/1280px-Justice_Democrats_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_Democrats\" target=\"_blank\"> Justice Democrats - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_Democrats\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_Democrats </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=zkdzpTQeZWs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=zkdzpTQeZWs\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=zkdzpTQeZWs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=zkdzpTQeZWs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is epic, hugely epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:59:51-08:00","id":1040294,"title":"","content":"That would be nice if were successful. Unfortunately, running for office takes a lot of money, so I don't expect very many Democrats to be lining up to ditch their political donations. If the Justice Democrats can't exert enough pressure to force Democrats to bow, most of them won't. And then, even if a bunch of Democrats did sign on, if they can't somehow make up the money they're losing from those political donations, they'll have a harder time winning elections.<br /> <br /> While this previous election cycle showed that you <i>can</i> win even without spending that much money, the reality is, money does make it easier to get elected. There's a number of reasons why many Democrats will resist this (some of those are even reasonable), and hopefully those who agree don't end up crippling their campaigns and losing elections because they didn't get enough money. If that happens, that would be the death of this movement. <br /> <br /> So there are some potential problems it that immediately stood out to me, and I imagine the Justice Democrats will have a huge uphill battle. But if this movement takes off, I think it would be fantastic for the Democratic Party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-30-2017, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:02:00-08:00","id":1040296,"title":"","content":"KayIGjfbGOKGrB6TTtzZwznOTb0SkGfD6ZlVzErhLhIlqTAsJU Vs0kuwpZC_lHs07LQAw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:06:41-08:00","id":1040299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1040296#post1040296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KayIGjfbGOKGrB6TTtzZwznOTb0SkGfD6ZlVzErhLhIlqTAsJU Vs0kuwpZC_lHs07LQAw</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you just stroke out? Should I call an ambulance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:58:56-08:00","id":1040423,"title":"","content":"That... Sounds... Pretty fucking rad, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:02:09-08:00","id":1040467,"title":"","content":"Guess some people really want to take the Centre out of Centre-Left Democrats.<br /> <br /> Will be interesting to see who wins that civil war, if one even starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 01-30-2017, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T01:42:06-08:00","id":1040493,"title":"","content":"Eh.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of good in there, but there's also some self-sabotage. Like not taking any money from billionaires. Why? Not all billionaires are the same. Warren Buffett gave to Clinton, but gave a good deal less than many millionaire donors do, because he completely agrees with the need to get financial reform of the election process. If Buffett gives a candidate $25K... that politician is going to face a primary on general principle of... what? All billionaires are evil? Or do people like Buffett who would probably support a lot of the Justice Democrat platform (if not all of it) have to give to the Justice Democrat leadership so they can distribute the money (which just sets them up to be the same sort of organization as the DNC anyway)? If a billionaire wants to help people get elected because they'll tax billionaires more, ensure money has less power over elections, and so on... what's the point of not letting them use their wealth to make that happen? Being &quot;bought&quot; by a billionaire for the sole purpose of making sure billionaires can't buy politicians doesn't exactly seem like a big moral compromise to me. Their platform even includes implementing the Buffett rule! So we'll follow your economic advice but not use your money to make it happen...<br /> <br /> Pressure for greater transparency among Democratic candidates? OK, that's a good standard. There's no self-sabotage there. If you want to give to the Democratic cause, you shouldn't be scared to let people know it, and they shouldn't be scared to let people know who the big donors are. <br /> <br /> I think there's another issue with getting support:<br /> <br /> Their platform isn't really that different from the main democratic platform. A lot of the differences are implementation ones (universal health care in pieces aka Obamacare vs. single payer, universal higher education vs. debt free higher education).<br /> <br /> So the big differences when you break it down are:<br /> <br /> Trade deals, though there stance seems to not really understand how trade deals work. Opposing bad trade deals is all well and good, but they have a key point backwards. Outsourcing happens because costs are cheaper somewhere else. That happens with or without trade deals. Good trade deals are the leverage to reduce the economic impact of that without getting into a trade war. If the Justice Democrats oppose trade deals completely, then what? If it's just, &quot;oppose bad trade deals, but use good ones,&quot; that's the Center Democrats party line already. Yelling about NAFTA is a useful tool for populism, but not really a great economic policy position (as Trump's administration seems to be learning).<br /> <br /> Military spending, but that seems to be more a matter of degree than not.<br /> <br /> Nation Building... though that seems to be something Center Democrats are toning down/backing off from anyway.<br /> <br /> Ranked Choice Voting, but that seems something of an odd thing to force on the federal level candidates. Federal level candidates can't force Ranked Choice on the States. That's got to be a local level thing, jurisdiction by jurisdiction. We're also seeing the first state wide Ranked Choice going into effect in 2018 anyway, with lots of smaller jurisdictions already adopting it (and most of them are largely Democratic leaning areas as it is). There doesn't really seem to be any significant Center Democrat opposition to this plank, just a lack of priority to it.<br /> <br /> It feels like this is going to be the Sanders Campaign all over again. The positions aren't so different or motivating to mirror the Tea Party successfully. I don't think the Democratic voter base is down enough with the &quot;purity&quot; primary and pushing that tactic too hard is going to be a problem. Do they seriously think they could go after someone like Elijah Cummings or John Lewis if they don't abide by the Justice Democrat purity tests? If John Lewis says, &quot;Warren Buffett can donate to my campaign like any other private citizen,&quot; the Justice Democrats are screwed. Trying to primary him is going to destroy their credibility with the mainstream Democratic voter, but not doing it means they don't have the backbone to go after anyone.<br /> <br /> There's no need to be absolutists in this. They can avoid all the problems with extremely popular Democrats that might not pass the strict purity test by having a score card system that says, &quot;we primary everyone that doesn't get an A- or better.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Tea Party strategy might have been really good for creating a power opposition, but it sucked for getting effective candidates elected that could actually govern to get all those platform ideals passed. The Freedom Caucus vs. the Republican leadership has been bad for the Republicans, not good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:17:14-08:00","id":1040574,"title":"","content":"I think if Warren Buffet gave a whooping $250 say, they'd give it a pass, the idea is billionaire shouldn't be in the business of buying politicians, it's about the ethics of the act of billionaire getting a politic in their debt that is the problem, it doesn't matter what policies they support, saying it's okay if a billionaire agrees, with us, but not if they don't is hypocracy, the rule has to be consistent or it undermines the whole thing. <br /> <br /> You can't ask one side to give up massive donations from the rich to get big money out of politics, then accept those types of donations because a billionaire happens to agree with your politics, the other side will rightly point out such hypocracy. <br /> <br /> The difference between single payer universal healthcare and Obamacare which is really Mittromneycare as I understand it, is absolutely massive. <br /> <br /> The difference between some debt relief for tuition and free public post secondary education is massive.<br /> <br /> Cutting reckless defence spending and stopping the destructive influence of the military industry complex isn't just a matter of degree, it's removing the driving force behind the endless parade of wars America finds itself in. <br /> <br /> These aren't piddly things, there utterly massive differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:25:54-08:00","id":1040579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1040299#post1040299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you just stroke out? Should I call an ambulance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No LMFAO, for some reason the copy paste of the link to their website didn't work properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:51:51-08:00","id":1040595,"title":"","content":"I'm cautiously down with this. I say &quot;cautiously,&quot; because I don't really know enough about macroeconomics to assess what the real effects of some of these policies would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:38:11-08:00","id":1040688,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm much less excited or interested. I see it as &quot;Hey Bernie Sanders was super-popular during the last election, lets set up a whole GROUP of people that can glom onto that sort of popular support but still be as party-biased as ever!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:57:30-08:00","id":1040771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1040574#post1040574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if Warren Buffet gave a whooping $250 say, they'd give it a pass, the idea is billionaire shouldn't be in the business of buying politicians, it's about the ethics of the act of billionaire getting a politic in their debt that is the problem, it doesn't matter what policies they support, saying it's okay if a billionaire agrees, with us, but not if they don't is hypocracy, the rule has to be consistent or it undermines the whole thing.<br /> <br /> You can't ask one side to give up massive donations from the rich to get big money out of politics, then accept those types of donations because a billionaire happens to agree with your politics, the other side will rightly point out such hypocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is the whole problem with the purity test ideology that the Tea Party model uses. You can't say, &quot;no money from billionaires&quot; and then cut Buffett some slack (that's also hypocrisy).<br /> <br /> That's why I call this self-sabotage. It's a symbolic purity test that doesn't actually equate to any practical assurance of results. It's also a completely arbitrary cut off point that makes for good talking points but bad policy. If I'm a Democratic candidate, I can avoid a primary challenge by refusing money from billionaires and corporations... and then get millions of campaign dollars from extremely wealthy millionaires instead.<br /> <br /> If the Justice Democrats are really serious about this, they should have a much more practical/meaningful test such as, &quot;our candidates pledge to be completely transparent in their donations, and to refuse donations in excess of the legal individual contribution limits from individuals that loopholes allow.&quot; That way Buffett can give his $25K (this is not a number I'm pulling out of thin air btw), and there's no hypocrisy.<br /> <br /> No dark money, and not using loopholes to get around donation caps is really what this ideology is about and should be what the test actually is. Not saying, &quot;billionaires and corporations!&quot; just because it sounds better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference between single payer universal healthcare and Obamacare which is really Mittromneycare as I understand it, is absolutely massive.<br /> <br /> The difference between some debt relief for tuition and free public post secondary education is massive. </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on what your goals are.<br /> <br /> If you want to try to enshrine healthcare/higher education as rights, the differences is massive.<br /> <br /> If you want to get good healthcare and affordable higher education to the maximum number of citizens... not so much.<br /> <br /> If you want to try to get at some of the systemic issues in the US system around these topics, either approach in both cases gives the federal government enough political power to assert itself for the good of the populace. We don't need single payer for the federal government to have standing/political power to address the ridiculous way medical services are priced. The US government already is the largest single insurance provider in the country, with all the leverage that allows on top of legislative power. We don't need free higher education to address the way the job markets have devalued a college/university degree and all the negative impacts that has on top of how expensive they are to get. Federal money is already on the line for many schools and business to step into that arena and address those problems. Job creation in middle class sectors plus lower student loan interest rates would drastically reduce the student debt problem without the debt-free vs tuition free debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cutting reckless defence spending and stopping the destructive influence of the military industry complex isn't just a matter of degree, it's removing the driving force behind the endless parade of wars America finds itself in. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reckless&quot; is a subjective standard which does make this a matter of degree.<br /> <br /> As well, most of the excessive military spending in the US federal budget has nothing to do with foreign wars. The DoD and associated bodies have consistently told Congress that they don't need all this money to do what they're being asked to do in regards to combat readiness and active deployment.<br /> <br /> Most of that money is actually about members of Congress creating jobs for their States/Districts. Large military bases = jobs for the local community. Tank factories that make tanks that are all mothballed immediately = factory jobs. A massive portion of the defense budget is really just a scheme to create socialized jobs without calling them government jobs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These aren't piddly things, there utterly massive differences. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you've demonstrated a comprehensive understanding of these issues to actually make that assessment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:26:34-08:00","id":1040811,"title":"","content":"I was referring to having a donation limit as opposed to directly banning Billionaires from donating. But I agree if it's an out right ban on donations from all billionaires then it has to apply even to ones allies. Warren Buffet will live he can give to the homeless, wounded war vets, or to fight climate change instead,ect...<br /> <br /> No offence but your disastrous healthcare system is the warning Canadians point to when some selfish asshole wants to privatize healthcare. <br /> <br /> It's time for universal healthcare in America, there is no excuse for the disaster you have, it not like there aren't models that work far better for you to emulate. <br /> <br /> So take that military money and build something useful with it, roads, hospitals, enviromental technology, research, manufacture stuff for the poor, ect... <br /> <br /> Look at the Canadian Healthcare system, which does have it's flaws, and heartbreaking mess America is in. <br /> <br /> There are a tons of information supporting single payer universal healthcare out there, too much for me to link to it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:19:09-08:00","id":1040893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1040811#post1040811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to having a donation limit as opposed to directly banning Billionaires from donating. But I agree if it's an out right ban on donations from all billionaires then it has to apply even to ones allies. Warren Buffet will live he can give to the homeless, wounded war vets, or to fight climate change instead,ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Having an outright ban on billionaires is still a dumb position. It's not like there's a ban on people worth between $100 and $999 million in this, and there's a lot of those to pick up the slack in violation of the ideology of the movement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No offence but your disastrous healthcare system is the warning Canadians point to when some selfish asshole wants to privatize healthcare. </div> </div> </div>No offense taken. Our healthcare system is shit. But the ACA did a huge amount to start to address it. The ACA isn't perfect, but as a framework it can address the issue of distributing insurance and reforming insurance standards. The issues in our system that aren't just about distributing insurance though. Things like addressing the aggressive increase in drug costs is not an issue of how we get people insurance. Combating the illogical price disparities where in two comparable hospitals operating in the same area charge radically different costs for the same thing. ACA vs. single payer, doesn't inherently fix that in one of those hospitals saline IV drips are $25 a bag, and $150 a bag in another; insurance companies don't write the charge sheets. The government doesn't need to be an insurance provider at all to step in and regulate charge sheets.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean about comprehensive understanding of the issues. You don't seem to have any depth of knowledge about where the cracks in the system actually are, and what measures are needed to fix them.<br /> <br /> I'm a supporter of single payer. I'd be overjoyed if we stopped putting health insurance company profits over ensuring a healthy populace. You don't need to sell me on it being what I would do if I could snap my fingers and change government policies.<br /> <br /> However, I also live in the USA. I have to deal with the laws that actually get passed. I will take the imperfect (and improvable) ACA over going back to before the ACA, The problem here isn't the left. The left is sold on universal healthcare being the right idea. The right, however, doesn't want it, and will take no health care reform and letting people die because they don't have enough money over it.<br /> <br /> Taking a purity stance on healthcare in the USA means screwing people like me over, because not accepting a compromise solution like the ACA means no healthcare reform at all until the Democrats have a solid and massive political mandate. &quot;Universal healthcare or nothing&quot; vs &quot;Private healthcare or nothing,&quot; means &quot;or nothing&quot; is going to win, and people like me are fucked.<br /> <br /> People's lives are on the line. This isn't something to be playing political chicken over. Fighting for a universal single payer system is a great cause. But primarying Democrats that want to fight to protect the ACA in the meantime to make sure people don't <b>die</b> until single payer can be a political reality is not the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So take that military money and build something useful with it, roads, hospitals, enviromental technology, research, manufacture stuff for the poor, ect... </div> </div> </div>I agree. The mainstream Democratic party agrees. That's why this is far more a matter of degree as I said before. The Democratic party is in general support of less defense spending and more spending and on everything you just listed. The Justice Democrats aren't adding anything new there, they're just pushing to make bigger cuts to defense than mainstream Democrats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:40:35-08:00","id":1040948,"title":"","content":"How did Obama's compromise solution pan out, oh wait it's being tossed in the trash by Trump, even though Republicans actually the ones who came up with it! That's the kind of crazy your dealing with. <br /> <br /> You can only make reason compromises with whose willing to recipericate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:26:07-08:00","id":1041028,"title":"","content":"And... the answer is to start a civil war on the left? The answer is to work to ensure we go back to people going bankrupt just to survive, and some not surviving at all, instead of doing what we can to minimize the damage on the horizon because minimizing the damage on the horizon isn't some people's preferred solution to healthcare reform? We need to do the same idiotic thing as the Republicans and go for &quot;Repeal and Replace,&quot; before we're ready to replace?<br /> <br /> We should can effective fighters for healthcare reform because they're not ideological purists to one particularly view of progressive politics? We should risk losing power in the Congress as Democrats in competitive districts/states lose to Republicans since far left Democrats win the primaries and lose elections (this happened repeatedly with the Tea Party)?<br /> <br /> And if Obama had managed to get single payer through the way the ACA got through... Trump could trash it now just the same. &quot;Single payer&quot; is not magically immune to repeal in US law.<br /> <br /> Also, even if I lose the protections I've gained, I've saved ~$10,000 already because of Obamacare. So it worked out really well for me. Even if I'm going to lose all that savings really fast in a year. It was at least a few years respite from demoralizing medical bills.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get it. You think America should go single payer. I do to. But I don't buy proper progressive politics is to help the Republicans to dismantle the ACA instead of impeding them as much as possible, so we can have single payer as a plank for some point in the future when single payer can actually get passed here.<br /> <br /> Getting single payer to happen means getting a lot of other work done first, and in the meantime ACA protection should be a concern of the party until single payer is a political reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:37:30-08:00","id":1041446,"title":"","content":"Some times you have to clean out the rot, it's not always pleasant, but it's needed. <br /> <br /> And honestly the Republicans had infighting all over the place last time and they won the both houses and the Presidentancy, and most of the governorships. <br /> <br /> No sacrifice no victory, witwicky moto (from Transformers)<br /> <br /> Nothing stops anyone from trying to impede Trump removing ACA, if anything the corporstists are the ones folding to Trumps wishes such as on his nominations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-31-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:48:29-08:00","id":1041452,"title":"","content":"When your &quot;not pleasant&quot; means ruining hundreds of thousands of people's lives, and enacting policies that will certainly ensure people die when we could have prevented it, just to score political points, you have no moral center to claim to rally the populace around you.<br /> <br /> Since you're willing to argue that letting people die is worth cleaning out this &quot;rot&quot; how many people should we just go out and kill to make sure it happens? No sacrifice, no victory right? How many deaths gets rid of the rot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-31-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:15:38-08:00","id":1041476,"title":"","content":"Also, a bit of a factual point. The Republicans <b>maintained control</b> over both houses. They've been losing seats since the Tea Party's success in taking them over, just not enough for control to flip back to the Democrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:32:52-08:00","id":1041522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1041452#post1041452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your &amp;quot;not pleasant&amp;quot; means ruining hundreds of thousands of people's lives, and enacting policies that will certainly ensure people die when we could have prevented it, just to score political points, you have no moral center to claim to rally the populace around you.<br /> <br /> Since you're willing to argue that letting people die is worth cleaning out this &amp;quot;rot&amp;quot; how many people should we just go out and kill to make sure it happens? No sacrifice, no victory right? How many deaths gets rid of the rot?</div> </div> </div> </div> Excuse me, at no point did I suggesting ruining thousands of peoples lives, it with fuck up some peoples ambitions, but it will lead to vast improvements to millions of peoples lives. <br /> <br /> &quot;Don't let anyone tell you it can't be done.&quot; Jack Layton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:06:17-08:00","id":1041546,"title":"","content":"Your response to, &quot;The way the Justice Democrats are phrasing their political ideology and tactics will ruin people's lives and even kill people indirectly, because of insisting on purity instead of acknowledging that some goals will take lots of ground work to accomplish,&quot; was, &quot;sometimes sacrifices are necessary.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fucking up some people's ambitions isn't worth that cost, and achieving the vast improvements you're talking about doesn't require it.<br /> <br /> I'm not telling you it can't be done. I'm telling you this is a stupid way to do it, and a morally dubious one at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:24:22-08:00","id":1041580,"title":"","content":"How exactly do you suggest it be done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:33:02-08:00","id":1041585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.washingtonpost.com/amphtml/news/post-politics/wp/2017/01/23/progressives-launch-justice-democrats-to-counter-primary-corporate-legislators/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.washingtonpost.com/amphtml/news/post-politics/wp/2017/01/23/progressives-launch-justice-democrats-to-counter-primary-corporate-legislators/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.washingtonpost.com/amphtml/news/post-politics/wp/2017/01/23/progressives-launch-justice-democrats-to-counter-primary-corporate-legislators/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.washingtonpost.com/amphtml/news/post-politics/wp/2017/01/23/progressives-launch-justice-democrats-to-counter-primary-corporate-legislators/?client=ms-android-bell-ca </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T00:37:52-08:00","id":1041727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1041580#post1041580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly do you suggest it be done?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Drop the self-sabotaging rhetoric. Don't set purity standards that are either going to bite you in the ass, or are not vital to your ideals. Bernie Sanders took money from billionaires and corporations too. Why didn't anyone attack him about that? Because his supporters <b>don't care</b>. Those billionaires and corporations were the &quot;good ones&quot; because they gave money to the &quot;right&quot; candidate. Again, focus on what really matters and what will resonate with people without setting yourself up to fail. Demand your candidates reject dark money, and have systems to ensure rich donors/corporations don't donate more than they're supposed to so you can show that you're not letting them buy you (something Sanders also failed to do even if it was never enough for anyone to really care about). Remember that the &quot;we don't have a SuperPAC&quot; line is meaningless and can be turned against you as SuperPACs can be created by your supporters to operate on your behalf (Sanders did have a SuperPAC, because he couldn't actually stop it from happening, and while Clinton wasn't going to denounce a bunch of nurses, Trump would have jumped on that).<br /> <br /> 2) Prove to the mainstream Democratic base you can grow the party politically before getting primary happy. Replacing all the &quot;corporate&quot; Democrats, even if you somehow keep seats in red leaning States that would likely reject a highly progressive candidate despite the issues if the Republicans run a more centrist candidate, leaves the party... not in control of the House or Senate, so none of the platform gets passed even if Trump is a one term president. Build a bench for 2018 that's more focused on winning open Democratic primaries (in the sense of there not being an incumbent Democrat) with progressive candidates that can win the actual election; esp. on local and state level elections. This is essential step for the long term goals in the first place, and creates a mandate for 2020 to get incumbent Democrats to move farther to the left to keep their positions or they get replaced. Five Republican Governors getting replaced by Justice Democrats is worth far more in every way than five centrist Democrat Congressmen being replaced with Justice Democrats. Otherwise we're back to the Clinton-Sanders race, and the centrist Democrats will eke out victories because more Democrats are scared of losing the gains we've made than they're worried about the appearance of conflicts on interest as Democrats take money from people they're campaigning to harm the bottom line of.<br /> <br /> 3) Use that momentum to continue to defend things like the ACA until the Justice Democrats control the Democratic Party, and the Democratic Party has regained control over the government.<br /> <br /> 4) Have actual policies ready to go. Not strong policy ideas. The laws need to be written to be submitted for review and consideration in legislatures before the next cycle in them. &quot;When we win, this is the exact law we're going to pass, get on board or get out of the way.&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Now that the Democrats are a solidly progressive party that's shown it's dedicated to it's populist ideology, grow the party until the Republicans stop having a say for at least a two-term president. Use that power to regulate things properly, replace stop gap efforts like the ACA with a <b>good</b> single payer system (and remind any Republicans that you're consolidating a few dozen programs into one program and making government smaller and more efficient to shut them up about your &quot;big government&quot; programs), and go to work on the big lifts in the platform that are going to run into a need to either go through the Courts or even face a need for Amendments (these are hard, you have to have a ton of political mandate to even hope to make these happen).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T04:50:25-08:00","id":1041765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1041585#post1041585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.washingtonpost.com/amphtml/news/post-politics/wp/2017/01/23/progressives-launch-justice-democrats-to-counter-primary-corporate-legislators/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.ca/amp/s/www.wash...ndroid-bell-ca</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I read this article, and I have to ask: by what metric is <i>Cory Booker</i> not &quot;progressive&quot; enough!?<br /> <br /> For that reason alone, I've come around to Heavy Arms' side. This movement looks like it's more likely to sabotage the Democratic party and further divide the nation than it is to accomplish anything useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:13:09-08:00","id":1041893,"title":"","content":"Well, despite everything I've said, if the Justice Democrats stay mostly focused on local/state elections, and &quot;save up&quot; their efforts for federal election for at least the next cycle (or a few more) they could have more positive impact than negative even if at some point there would have to be a reconciliation between them and the DNC when it comes to the federal elections to avoid the in-fighting the Republicans are dealing with; and who the head of the DNC is, is going to matter a lot.<br /> <br /> This is esp, true if they work up a solid strategy in two key areas: getting the right candidates into the Rust Belt states and Coal Country where a more shallow populist message will work as long as it gets results (which the Sanders crowd contributors to the Justice Democrats have a lot of tools for doing), and establishing a better movement in the South to finally undo the Southern Strategy (which the current leaders of the Justice Democrats have shown absolutely zero skill at).<br /> <br /> These are both areas of the country where numerically speaking the left/progressives should have a slight but significant advantage and be not just purple-blue on the federal level, but be pretty blue on the state/local level. Right now they're very red on the state/local level. That's a huge problem, especially towards things like voting reform or eventually getting constitutional amendments passed. Regardless of why you think the Democrats are failing to get these votes the failure to do that is one of the biggest hurdles the Democrats have had in enacting a progressive agenda since the third year of the Obama administration.<br /> <br /> As I've harped on before in political threads, a great example of the Sanders people failing on this is in Pennsylvania's Senate election and the chance to unseat Pat Toomey. We had a perfect candidate: a popular mayor of a city that was slammed by the recession, progressive that showed how progressive policies helped his city bounce back, a Sanders supporter, an outsider without the super wealthy donors or megacorporate backers. The problem? No support. The DNC wanted their mainstream Democrat, and the Sanders people weren't paying enough attention to PA to even know about the guy before Sanders was in PA getting interviewed, and found out about him when asked. So we got boringly standard Democrat A instead of boring standard Democrat B (which probably wasn't even the best choice tactically even if she was slightly more progressive than he was, he had a cleaner record and the veteran sympathy vote), and boringly standard Democrat A lost a, &quot;who's the bigger corporate stooge&quot; fight with Toomey. This is where we need the Justice Democrats to really act and mobilize, because the DNC isn't doing it.<br /> <br /> If the Justice Democrats can reverse that, a certain amount of strife with the mainstream Democrats is worth it. <br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Also, on the Cory Booker thing, even if you don't think he passes your progressive purity test... going after him is dumb. Senators have to win their elections by getting majority support in their states. That means more people in New Jersey voted for Booker than anyone else. That's why the Tea Party had almost no traction in primarying Republican Senators (most of the Tea Party Senators are converts or beat Democrats to get there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:23:11-08:00","id":1042028,"title":"","content":"Not all swing voters think in leftwing vs. right wing terms, there are republican voters who will vote for afar left socialist if they believe that socialist cares and has integrity, so don't assume that centralists are more prepared to win swing votes then progressives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:42:26-08:00","id":1042041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042028#post1042028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all swing voters think in leftwing vs. right wing terms, there are republican voters who will vote for afar left socialist if they believe that socialist cares and has integrity, so don't assume that centralists are more prepared to win swing votes then progressives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassion and integrity alone won't automatically overcome ideological mistrust. What's needed in the areas we're talking about is a cogent platform tailored to addressing the problems that are actually relevant to the lives of the people there. Whether or not such a platform will actually bear any resemblance to right/left political orthodoxy is an open question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:03:43-08:00","id":1042121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042028#post1042028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all swing voters think in leftwing vs. right wing terms, there are republican voters who will vote for afar left socialist if they believe that socialist cares and has integrity, so don't assume that centralists are more prepared to win swing votes then progressives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm extrapolating based on what I saw during the Tea Party movement (which is the model the Justice Democrats say they want to recreate).<br /> <br /> I grew up in a state that's not thought of as a swing state because it leans Democrat and has gone Democrat for President for seven straight elections (though was solidly Republican for a long time before that). For the Congress and the Senate, it has a much more diverse history during the last 30 years.... until the Tea Party drove it solidly Democrat for every election since because they primaried a beloved Republican Congressman. I'm talking a guy that regularly got 65-70% of the vote in a blue-leaning state because he had such a good reputation with Democratic voters. Democrats in the state a largely rejected the Republicans for a decade because of it thoroughout the state and for federal elections.<br /> <br /> This is why purity primaries are dangerous.<br /> <br /> Centrists are often better prepared to win swing votes because they've already been doing it. Again, this is why the Tea Party had far less impact on the Senate than the House. Senators that aren't in heavily party-aligned states succeed because they can get swing votes better than their opponents. A lot of them can do it because at least in their state, they're really popular (like Cory Booker). The Tea Party was successful because they could target Representatives in &quot;safe&quot; districts where a Democrat didn't stand a chance, even against &quot;weak&quot; Republicans and going hard to the right could work.<br /> <br /> Don't assume that centrists aren't capable of of demonstrating caring and integrity to their constituents either. Sure there's an &quot;establishment = corrupt and uncaring&quot; feeling in the US right now, but that doesn't mean you can tar every incumbent/centrist with that rhetoric successfully.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:30:17-08:00","id":1042127,"title":"","content":"If the centrists are so great why be afraid of a democractic challenge? If they have to state solo locked down surely they can handle a Democratic challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:33:08-08:00","id":1042129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042121#post1042121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm extrapolating based on what I saw during the Tea Party movement (which is the model the Justice Democrats say they want to recreate).<br /> <br /> I grew up in a state that's not thought of as a swing state because it leans Democrat and has gone Democrat for President for seven straight elections (though was solidly Republican for a long time before that). For the Congress and the Senate, it has a much more diverse history during the last 30 years.... until the Tea Party drove it solidly Democrat for every election since because they primaried a beloved Republican Congressman. I'm talking a guy that regularly got 65-70% of the vote in a blue-leaning state because he had such a good reputation with Democratic voters. Democrats in the state a largely rejected the Republicans for a decade because of it thoroughout the state and for federal elections.<br /> <br /> This is why purity primaries are dangerous.<br /> <br /> Centrists are often better prepared to win swing votes because they've already been doing it. Again, this is why the Tea Party had far less impact on the Senate than the House. Senators that aren't in heavily party-aligned states succeed because they can get swing votes better than their opponents. A lot of them can do it because at least in their state, they're really popular (like Cory Booker). The Tea Party was successful because they could target Representatives in &amp;quot;safe&amp;quot; districts where a Democrat didn't stand a chance, even against &amp;quot;weak&amp;quot; Republicans and going hard to the right could work.<br /> <br /> Don't assume that centrists aren't capable of of demonstrating caring and integrity to their constituents either. Sure there's an &amp;quot;establishment = corrupt and uncaring&amp;quot; feeling in the US right now, but that doesn't mean you can tar every incumbent/centrist with that rhetoric successfully.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've seen enough centerists sell out time and again, to know that the ones who don't are a rare breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:41:46-08:00","id":1042136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042127#post1042127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the centrists are so great why be afraid of a democractic challenge? If they have to state solo locked down surely they can handle a Democratic challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the last time we had a centrist with things &quot;locked down&quot; and there was still a faction of disaffected democrats running around, Ol' Donny Boy won the election. And <i>he </i>was mostly riding on the accomplishments of an earlier splinter faction that was unseating the establishment centrists of the Republican party.<br /> <br /> So, I see two problems here.<br /> 1. A unified party is tautologically stronger than an disunified party. Factional infighting is something we cannot afford during this period when we have a majority Republican House, Senate, and Executive branch, and blithely assuming it'll all work out in 2018 or 2020 strikes me as very naive.<br /> 2. As we have seen/are seeing, intentional ideological extremism can easily twist a political party into a sick parody of itself.<br /> <br /> I miss Milton Friedman...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042129#post1042129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen enough centerists sell out time and again, to know that the ones who don't are a rare breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You call it &quot;selling out.&quot; I call it &quot;compromising to serve the many interests of a diverse group of people&quot;, which is what I would generally hope for from our government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-01-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:50:41-08:00","id":1042162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042136#post1042136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the last time we had a centrist with things &amp;quot;locked down&amp;quot; and there was still a faction of disaffected democrats running around, Ol' Donny Boy won the election. And <i>he </i>was mostly riding on the accomplishments of an earlier splinter faction that was unseating the establishment centrists of the Republican party.<br /> <br /> So, I see two problems here.<br /> 1. A unified party is tautologically stronger than an disunified party. Factional infighting is something we cannot afford during this period when we have a majority Republican House, Senate, and Executive branch, and blithely assuming it'll all work out in 2018 or 2020 strikes me as very naive.<br /> 2. As we have seen/are seeing, intentional ideological extremism can easily twist a political party into a sick parody of itself.<br /> <br /> I miss Milton Friedman...<br /> <br /> <br /> You call it &amp;quot;selling out.&amp;quot; I call it &amp;quot;compromising to serve the many interests of a diverse group of people&amp;quot;, which is what I would generally hope for from our government.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call it being bought and payed for, which it what it is.<br /> <br /> Look the justice democracts aren't going anywhere just because you think progressives should shut up and let the corporatists get away with whatever they want. <br /> <br /> I've been effectively told my whole life by centrists that I had to ignore betrayal after betrayal and support the center right Liberal party in my country, so the right didn't win, I voted NDP instead, and I was proven right about the Liberal Party time and again.<br /> <br /> The age when progressive fallen in line and obey the centists so the booey men doesn't get them is over. <br /> <br /> And it was the centrists in the Democratic party that pushed the disaster Hillary Clinton on America, so Donald Trump is on them, not progressives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:42:20-08:00","id":1042183,"title":"","content":"I am not going to have yet another dogma-off with you. If you have other research or articles to present, present them. Otherwise, I'm done here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:45:04-08:00","id":1042184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042129#post1042129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen enough centerists sell out time and again, to know that the ones who don't are a rare breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love how you respond to a specific example with vague unfalsifiable dodging. You should really stop wasting your time here and go be a sellout politician; you've already got the main tactic down.<br /> <br /> If you want to demonstrate knowledge about our political climate and our current politicians, you need to step it up a bit. Otherwise you're just reminding us that if a Young Turk posts something on the Internet, you take it as gospel truth without any examination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042162#post1042162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I call it being bought and payed for, which it what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please provide an actual counter-example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look the justice democracts aren't going anywhere just because you think progressives should shut up and let the corporatists get away with whatever they want. </div> </div> </div>And this is the exact sort of nonsense the left in the US <b>does not need</b>.<br /> <br /> This is the problem with purity politics.<br /> <br /> We point out flaws in the Justice Democrats' statements, and when your attempt to defend them doesn't go well... suddenly we want progressives to shut up and we're corporate stooges.<br /> <br /> When did the Justice Democrats become the sole voice of what counts as progressive? Since when did I have to suck their dicks to not be labelled as a &quot;corporatist?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is bad for progressives, because the progressives <b>need</b> the more moderate and centrist Democrats to get anything done. There are not enough sympathetic votes out their from anyone else. Like <b>any parliamentary system in the rest of the world</b> if you need to form a coalition, you have to compromise with your partners. That means the progressives need to compromise with the centrists. Labeling anybody that's not pure enough &quot;evil&quot; with whatever codeword you want to use is not coalition building.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been effectively told my whole life by centrists that I had to ignore betrayal after betrayal and support the center right Liberal party in my country, so the right didn't win, I voted NDP instead, and I was proven right about the Liberal Party time and again. </div> </div> </div>That sucks. We're not you. You're talking about American politics, not Canadian politics, so your experiences aren't directly relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it was the centrists in the Democratic party that pushed the disaster Hillary Clinton on America, so Donald Trump is on them, not progressives. </div> </div> </div>Fun fact, Clinton spent more time pushing universal single payer health care than Sanders ever has, and the reason you think so poorly of her is pretty much guaranteed to be significantly impacted by the huge amount of lies the US right pushed into the conversation about her to discredit her and spot single payer.<br /> <br /> And that was before she was elected by anyone, and therefore wasn't bought by anyone because she wasn't raising money from anyone for herself.<br /> <br /> Things are not black and white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T22:31:05-08:00","id":1042235,"title":"","content":"My own thoughts/observations.<br /> <br /> The Young Turks, and the person specifically boosting this plan have managed/run a Superpac in the past specifically to support democratic candidates... so they've clearly got no illusions that the biggest money bag wins the election. This makes me wary of that whole side of things.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Young Turks have an established history of biased reporting, usually with a pro-democrat slant. The whole &quot;See the anarchists smashing stuff?!!? They're anti-trump protesters! See how horrible The Other Side is?!!?&quot; that was done by the conservative media? The Young Turks were doing *exactly* the same thing 8 years ago. So they're not Shining Warriors of Justice And Correctness, they're just as manipulative... just with a different slant, targeting a different audience.<br /> <br /> I would argue that Sanders did spend a LOT of time on the universal healthcare push, since he was a major backer of Clinton's push back when her husband was in office. Not as much as Clinton I will agree, but that's also the difference between the political risks a senator can take vs the first lady.<br /> <br /> I do agree that health care needs further reform, a single payer system would be grand, but likewise agree that repealing the ACA is NOT in any way step in that direction... the ACA added certain key protections that if removed will have significant problems, like the pre-existing condition clauses. If anyone wants a breakdown of the actual problems faced by the US health care systems I believe John Green has done several videos on youtube that cover them at a basic level.<br /> <br /> On the example of Tank construction for useless instantly mothballed tanks... It's actually something of a double-edged problem. It's not JUST keeping people employed, the problem is that it would be *more* expensive to fire the people than keep them on. The problem there is that in order to maintain a ready capacity to manufacture military vehicles you need to keep people around that know HOW to do it. Like many jobs there's a lot of knowledge that can't be simply dumped into a training manual that someone can read and do the job perfectly just from the manual. So they reduce the staff to a minimum production level, keeping just enough people around that you're not losing critical knowledge and you've got people that can train others if a need for production arises. If you *don't* do that, and you suddenly need to train people from nothing, with them learning elements not documented or clearly teachable as they go, you get a much higher ramp up time. <br /> <br /> The other thing to consider with that &quot;military industrial complex&quot; spending is that it's not like companies are taking all the money, pocketing it and doing nothing. Granted in many cases things can be streamlined, but ultimately those companies are employing workers skilled and semi-skilled, to do things. And since they're tied to the military, that means it's american citizens (or green-card holders) doing the work, most typically in the US itself. In other words, cutting that &quot;pork barrel spending&quot; means cutting middle class jobs. A lot of them. So it's something you want to ease into rather than hack and slash.<br /> <br /> Cutting out things so that something better can be built on top of it doesn't work in politics. You want an example of this? I've got one. Dan Quayle, former vice president of the US best known for incorrectly correcting a kid in a spelling bee on spelling the potato(e) actually did something else while in office. The paperwork reduction act of 1995. It was a simple and lovely idea, take a large amount of paperwork, convoluted regulations, put in newer, cleaner more straight forward rules and cut out the old. This eliminated some largely pointless things like the requirement to structurally test ashtrays in government buildings (where smoking wasn't allowed anymore). Something that helps everyone right? The end result was that the new regulations went into effect, and then it got reconned that the old regulations could not be removed. Because politics. Short of open revolution and rebuilding a system of law and government from scratch, government systems do NOT get more straightforward, they only get more convoluted. And even then, that doesn't usually happen. As an example I offer up one of the collection of laws that's causing headache these days... Civil Asset Forfeiture. This is the fun thing where the police can claim your property (money, home, vehicle etc) is suspect of being involved in a crime and take it. You know what the federal root of those laws are? England. They're English laws that after the american revolution the newly independent nation opted to keep because hey, it's already there and it's useful. Of course it has drifted since then, been applied to the state level and then abused/changed to deal with issues of the day, but that's where it came from.<br /> <br /> As for the Canadian vs the American politics, they have one major thing in common... it sucks. Major parties want power, they'll always try to appeal to as many people as they can swing, and this will happen until they do something to cause it to all come tumbling down. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T23:08:54-08:00","id":1042245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042162#post1042162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it was the centrists in the Democratic party that pushed the disaster Hillary Clinton on America, so Donald Trump is on them, not progressives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any &quot;progressives&quot; who refused to vote for Clinton on half-baked ideological grounds, of which I know more than a few, are every bit as much to blame for Trump. <br /> <br /> I voted for Sanders in the primary because I had a litany of problems with Clinton and I liked that Sanders' platform, achievability aside, would at least do something to slow the three decade rightward slide of the American political landscape. When everything shook out though and it was Clinton versus Trump I sucked it the fuck up and campaigned for Clinton because I could not conscience permitting a Trump presidency if there was any effort I could expend to stop it. <br /> <br /> Objection to a lesser evil does not justify acquiescence to a greater one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:06:45-08:00","id":1042260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042184#post1042184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love how you respond to a specific example with vague unfalsifiable dodging. You should really stop wasting your time here and go be a sellout politician; you've already got the main tactic down.<br /> <br /> If you want to demonstrate knowledge about our political climate and our current politicians, you need to step it up a bit. Otherwise you're just reminding us that if a Young Turk posts something on the Internet, you take it as gospel truth without any examination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please provide an actual counter-example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And this is the exact sort of nonsense the left in the US <b>does not need</b>.<br /> <br /> This is the problem with purity politics.<br /> <br /> We point out flaws in the Justice Democrats' statements, and when your attempt to defend them doesn't go well... suddenly we want progressives to shut up and we're corporate stooges.<br /> <br /> When did the Justice Democrats become the sole voice of what counts as progressive? Since when did I have to suck their dicks to not be labelled as a &amp;quot;corporatist?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> This is bad for progressives, because the progressives <b>need</b> the more moderate and centrist Democrats to get anything done. There are not enough sympathetic votes out their from anyone else. Like <b>any parliamentary system in the rest of the world</b> if you need to form a coalition, you have to compromise with your partners. That means the progressives need to compromise with the centrists. Labeling anybody that's not pure enough &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; with whatever codeword you want to use is not coalition building.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That sucks. We're not you. You're talking about American politics, not Canadian politics, so your experiences aren't directly relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fun fact, Clinton spent more time pushing universal single payer health care than Sanders ever has, and the reason you think so poorly of her is pretty much guaranteed to be significantly impacted by the huge amount of lies the US right pushed into the conversation about her to discredit her and spot single payer.<br /> <br /> And that was before she was elected by anyone, and therefore wasn't bought by anyone because she wasn't raising money from anyone for herself.<br /> <br /> Things are not black and white.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your right, your not Canada, your far worse, the Corporist Democracts get away with things that the Liberal Party of Canada can only dream of. <br /> <br /> It's late, but I'll gather some examples for corporate democracy's corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T03:17:05-08:00","id":1042321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042260#post1042260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your right, your not Canada, your far worse,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sick burn bro. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...the Corporist Democracts... </div> </div> </div>Please remember to not use this term in your research. &quot;Corporatism&quot; in politics was a <b>good thing</b> to progressives until ~10 years ago when people that had no idea it was already a thing misappropriated it to mean, &quot;crony capitalism.&quot; Most modern Western progressives are corporatists, and most of the Justice Democrat platform is based on corporatist values. It means something very different from how you're using it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T05:55:22-08:00","id":1042362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042321#post1042321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sick burn bro.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please remember to not use this term in your research. &quot;Corporatism&quot; in politics was a <b>good thing</b> to progressives until ~10 years ago when people that had no idea it was already a thing misappropriated it to mean, &quot;crony capitalism.&quot; Most modern Western progressives are corporatists, and most of the Justice Democrat platform is based on corporatist values. It means something very different from how you're using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neo-liberalism is bad and always has been bad. Progressives support it because it supports upper class republicans and democrats. I hate when people talk about politics. It's always abortion, minority rights or immigration it's never focused on government spending or corporate abuse. two of the things that dictate the actual flow of the fuckin federal government itself. The only difference between the two parties are superficial. It's why I stop caring about politics in the first place. Both sides are in the pockets of big corporations at this point and trump won't change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:56:40-08:00","id":1042454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042321#post1042321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sick burn bro. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please remember to not use this term in your research. &amp;quot;Corporatism&amp;quot; in politics was a <b>good thing</b> to progressives until ~10 years ago when people that had no idea it was already a thing misappropriated it to mean, &amp;quot;crony capitalism.&amp;quot; Most modern Western progressives are corporatists, and most of the Justice Democrat platform is based on corporatist values. It means something very different from how you're using it.</div> </div> </div> </div> It wasn't intended as a burn, it was concern, in Canada we point to the American Healthcare system as a cautionary tale of what not to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omega