blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=aM0kPGukpEQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=aM0kPGukpEQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here is a link to the discussion between Sargon of Akkad and Kyle of Secular Talk about Justice Democracts (which someone else brought up) that should address Epimetheus' concerns as well as provide some examples of corporate democracts corruption.<br /> <br /> It also shows why Kyle is so important, he is the one who will keep them focused on universality instead of the temptation to go towards more divisive identity politics, he even explains why minority issues are better addressed by universality in many cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-02-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:18:50-08:00","id":1042468,"title":"","content":"Being lectured on American progressivism by a Canadian MRA. The novelties of my week are truly without end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:44:46-08:00","id":1042481,"title":"","content":"Sargon's about as reliable a source as 2001 Wikipedia. Next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:54:42-08:00","id":1042536,"title":"","content":"Y'know, at least this thread prompted me to check if Cenk was still denying that the Armenian Genocide happened. Seems he's moved from denial to no-comment.<br /> <br /> Well! That's progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:52:11-08:00","id":1042558,"title":"","content":"Man, I recently started watching The Young Turks and I was diggin' their stuff. Not fond of the bias, and here I was thinking that I was getting better informed. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:33:09-08:00","id":1042572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042362#post1042362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neo-liberalism is bad and always has been bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all well and good, but the traditional meaning of corporatism does not make it the same thing as neo-liberalism.<br /> <br /> Do you want politicians to support stronger vocational and trade unions, and similar collective citizen organizations as a counter to the power of the wealthy and corporations?<br /> <br /> That means in traditional poli-sci definitions, you're a corporatist. Corporatism in traditional terms is the belief that collective citizen organizations should have a strong place in politics. Progressives have traditionally embraced corporatism based values because it means empowering common citizens to for politically active citizen organizations to use numbers in a democracy to push against the power that collects in the hands of the wealthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hate when people talk about politics. It's always abortion, minority rights or immigration it's never focused on government spending or corporate abuse. two of the things that dictate the actual flow of the fuckin federal government itself. </div> </div> </div> I hate it when people my gross and dismissive generalizations about things that can be shown to be false with a simple Google search. There's a lot of political conversations out there around spending and corporate power. Now, I can see a decent frustration about the lack of depth in many of these conversations, but they tend to get wonky very quickly which turns a lot of people off (and then doesn't get a lot of public attention).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only difference between the two parties are superficial. </div> </div> </div>I find this sort of thing frustrating.<br /> <br /> It's not true, but the impression has a valid source. The US political system was designed to pressure the government towards centrist/compromise policies. The whole idea was that no matter how far about the primary political blocs are in US politics, the system is meant to pull them together. This, of course, means that the results make them look &quot;samey&quot; because they're compromising to get laws passed in a system that assumes well deliberated laws that seek to use the best ideas of each political ideology at the table will in aggregate get the best laws.<br /> <br /> That intent isn't working out all that well right now, but that doesn't mean the parties are really the same with some minor differences. They're just working in the same system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042454#post1042454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't intended as a burn, it was concern, in Canada we point to the American Healthcare system as a cautionary tale of what not to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that, &quot;It's not meant to be insulting, but we denigrate your country to shame people in our country away from specific policy concerns,&quot; is still insulting my country, right?<br /> <br /> You're also dodging around again. I was pointing to your issues with Canadian parliamentary politics having the progressive party in the coalition not getting a fair deal out of the liberal party in terms of policy concessions not being directly applicable to the US Democratic party's issues. While the progressive wing of the party might be dissatisfied (though a lot of it is displaced anger over the general backslide we've been seeing on local/state races) on many fronts, they've gotten much larger say in the Democratic platform under Obama an in the 2016 campaign than there's been since the 60s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042457#post1042457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a link to the discussion between Sargon of Akkad and Kyle of Secular Talk about Justice Democracts (which someone else brought up) that should address Epimetheus' concerns as well as provide some examples of corporate democracts corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not listening to almost 3 hours of that. I gave it 15 minutes. But it became abundantly clear that Sargon's only there to softball to Kyle and then they can stroke each other's egos about how awesome they are for agreeing with each other. That's not a discussion. If I'm going to listen to an interview, especially one that long, I want the interviewer to actually press topics of concern. Even if the whole point is to give Kyle a platform to answer them without too much push back or a third party to debate things, I'd like to at least see some Devil's Advocate going on; because that's when we get to the real important stuff about the Justice Democrats and what they're really about. If it's just going to be another two and a half hours of, &quot;tell me about your other talking points.&quot; I don't care.<br /> <br /> I also don't consider either of them people of authority or solid journalistic credentials to be citing as &quot;research&quot; on corruption within the Democratic party in general, let alone the specifics of the power of corporations in American politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also shows why Kyle is so important, he is the one who will keep them focused on universality instead of the temptation to go towards more divisive identity politics, he even explains why minority issues are better addressed by universality in many cases. </div> </div> </div>Odd, within 15 minutes I could tell that he's incredibly wrong about important issues.<br /> <br /> They both seem to agree that the identity politics necessary during the Civil Rights movement were necessary, but then act as if that chapter of American history ended with a few bills getting passed.<br /> <br /> There is currently a school desegregation case pending federal appeals. Right now. In 2017. The federal courts are dealing with a city in Mississippi that is refusing to desegregate its schools. So... is the Civil Rights movement really over if we're still fighting this stuff over 50 years later?<br /> <br /> It's that sort of political myopia that troubles me about this sort of rhetoric. I think there's a valid point that significant factions within the Democratic Party have lost the messaging war in regards to identity politics and how we talk about them in political discourse as the left needs to be debated and considered more carefully. But you can't acknowledge the necessity of identity politics in the Civil Rights era, and then basically claim that we're post-racial now so we need to shut up about that stuff.<br /> <br /> Universality is good, but it's more complicated than Kyle make it out to be. Justice Democrats can't end up coming off to people of color as trading one type of identity politics for another by acting like all the social ills of today are color-blind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:25:59-08:00","id":1043085,"title":"","content":"Look you clearly know what Justice Democracts means when they say corporists, they are referring to cor