e 60s.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not listening to almost 3 hours of that. I gave it 15 minutes. But it became abundantly clear that Sargon's only there to softball to Kyle and then they can stroke each other's egos about how awesome they are for agreeing with each other. That's not a discussion. If I'm going to listen to an interview, especially one that long, I want the interviewer to actually press topics of concern. Even if the whole point is to give Kyle a platform to answer them without too much push back or a third party to debate things, I'd like to at least see some Devil's Advocate going on; because that's when we get to the real important stuff about the Justice Democrats and what they're really about. If it's just going to be another two and a half hours of, &amp;quot;tell me about your other talking points.&amp;quot; I don't care.<br /> <br /> I also don't consider either of them people of authority or solid journalistic credentials to be citing as &amp;quot;research&amp;quot; on corruption within the Democratic party in general, let alone the specifics of the power of corporations in American politics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Odd, within 15 minutes I could tell that he's incredibly wrong about important issues.<br /> <br /> They both seem to agree that the identity politics necessary during the Civil Rights movement were necessary, but then act as if that chapter of American history ended with a few bills getting passed.<br /> <br /> There is currently a school desegregation case pending federal appeals. Right now. In 2017. The federal courts are dealing with a city in Mississippi that is refusing to desegregate its schools. So... is the Civil Rights movement really over if we're still fighting this stuff over 50 years later?<br /> <br /> It's that sort of political myopia that troubles me about this sort of rhetoric. I think there's a valid point that significant factions within the Democratic Party have lost the messaging war in regards to identity politics and how we talk about them in political discourse as the left needs to be debated and considered more carefully. But you can't acknowledge the necessity of identity politics in the Civil Rights era, and then basically claim that we're post-racial now so we need to shut up about that stuff.<br /> <br /> Universality is good, but it's more complicated than Kyle make it out to be. Justice Democrats can't end up coming off to people of color as trading one type of identity politics for another by acting like all the social ills of today are color-blind.</div> </div> </div> </div> No ones suggesting that, they're just saying working on common issues is the best way to address them. <br /> <br /> I'm an MRA, nothing in the platform directly calls out go men in particular as being directly called a men's issue, but I'm smart enough to see how many of these issues disportionately effect men, like gun violence, so I don't need Kyle to call men out as being especially effected by that, I all ready know that, I feel no need to try and exclude women effected by it, just because it effects men more proportionally then women by a large margin, and I could point to other issues like that. <br /> <br /> It's about bring people together, not pulling them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:43:11-08:00","id":1043154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043085#post1043085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look you clearly know what Justice Democracts means when they say corporists, they are referring to corrupt politicians in the pockets of big business, not what your talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Words have meanings. A few Internet people on the left deciding to use a word without bothering to check what it actually means isn't something I feel strongly compelled to accept.<br /> <br /> Last time I check a good number of the founders of the Justice Democrats are people that should have known this (you know with things like Poli-Sci degrees), and them perpetuating it only adds to my impression that they're looking for clever slogans more than good policies. It's just like the &quot;no money from billionaires and corporations!&quot; line. It's propaganda, to rile up the already dissatisfied left, not talk that's productive to more than that.<br /> <br /> We have words for what they want to say, they don't need to turn another word into something meaningless because it has so many contradictory meanings that nobody cares anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043091#post1043091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No ones suggesting that, they're just saying working on common issues is the best way to address them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, at least Sargon and Kyle were pretty clear in that link you posted that they feel that the conditions of the past are over and thus the politics of the past need to be dropped. Which is fairly directly in contradiction of non-alternative-facts where many conditions of the past have yet to go away; thus the politics of them are not over either.<br /> <br /> Which is also kind of funny considering their official platform still engages in identity politics in places... so at least the rest of the Justice Democrats seem to recognize that Kyle's statements in that moment weren't on point. They specifically call for things that are not matters of universality; such as sexuality and gender based amendments to ensure their status as protected groups along with ethnicity, religion, and so on. There's a plank about fighting for women's rights. One of the planks has a more universality focused tone, but then calls out specific policies for their discriminatory nature. <br /> <br /> So yeah, the Justice Democrats as a whole might have their heads on their shoulders in this regard, even if Kyle discussed it poorly... and since I was talking about Kyle and your statement about how important his voice is, not their movement as a whole, I think my points still stand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's about bring people together, not pulling them apart. </div> </div> </div>That's what it should be about yes. That doesn't mean Kyle or Sargon are good messengers for it, or that the Justice Democrats as a whole have a solid grasp on how to accomplish this.<br /> <br /> The self-sabotaging rhetoric is a problem for this goal. Bringing people together means... also bringing the wealthy and powerful together with the rest of us. Yes, we need to make sure they're helping not &quot;leading&quot; but rejecting them completely is not a form of bringing people together.<br /> <br /> The purity primary tactic is a problem for this goal. That's tossing people out rather than bringing them together.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> We're also still waiting for this evidence thing you were going to provide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:31:00-08:00","id":1043650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043154#post1043154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Words have meanings. A few Internet people on the left deciding to use a word without bothering to check what it actually means isn't something I feel strongly compelled to accept.<br /> <br /> Last time I check a good number of the founders of the Justice Democrats are people that should have known this (you know with things like Poli-Sci degrees), and them perpetuating it only adds to my impression that they're looking for clever slogans more than good policies. It's just like the &amp;quot;no money from billionaires and corporations!&amp;quot; line. It's propaganda, to rile up the already dissatisfied left, not talk that's productive to more than that.<br /> <br /> We have words for what they want to say, they don't need to turn another word into something meaningless because it has so many contradictory meanings that nobody cares anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, at least Sargon and Kyle were pretty clear in that link you posted that they feel that the conditions of the past are over and thus the politics of the past need to be dropped. Which is fairly directly in contradiction of non-alternative-facts where many conditions of the past have yet to go away; thus the politics of them are not over either.<br /> <br /> Which is also kind of funny considering their official platform still engages in identity politics in places... so at least the rest of the Justice Democrats seem to recognize that Kyle's statements in that moment weren't on point. They specifically call for things that are not matters of universality; such as sexuality and gender based amendments to ensure their status as protected groups along with ethnicity, religion, and so on. There's a plank about fighting for women's rights. One of the planks has a more universality focused tone, but then calls out specific policies for their discriminatory nature. <br /> <br /> So yeah, the Justice Democrats as a whole might have their heads on their shoulders in this regard, even if Kyle discussed it poorly... and since I was talking about Kyle and your statement about how important his voice is, not their movement as a whole, I think my points still stand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's what it should be about yes. That doesn't mean Kyle or Sargon are good messengers for it, or that the Justice Democrats as a whole have a solid grasp on how to accomplish this.<br /> <br /> The self-sabotaging rhetoric is a problem for this goal. Bringing people together means... also bringing the wealthy and powerful together with the rest of us. Yes, we need to make sure they're helping not &amp;quot;leading&amp;quot; but rejecting them completely is not a form of bringing people together.<br /> <br /> The purity primary tactic is a problem for this goal. That's tossing people out rather than bringing them together.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> We're also still waiting for this evidence thing you were going to provide.</div> </div> </div> </div> Words have meaning, the excuse people use to over react to everything. ACTIONS have meaning, words have inturpratations the are skewed by the listeners personality and beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:11:17-08:00","id":1043670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043154#post1043154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Words have meanings. A few Internet people on the left deciding to use a word without bothering to check what it actually means isn't something I feel strongly compelled to accept.<br /> <br /> Last time I check a good number of the founders of the Justice Democrats are people that should have known this (you know with things like Poli-Sci degrees), and them perpetuating it only adds to my impression that they're looking for clever slogans more than good policies. It's just like the &amp;quot;no money from billionaires and corporations!&amp;quot; line. It's propaganda, to rile up the already dissatisfied left, not talk that's productive to more than that.<br /> <br /> We have words for what they want to say, they don't need to turn another word into something meaningless because it has so many contradictory meanings that nobody cares anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, at least Sargon and Kyle were pretty clear in that link you posted that they feel that the conditions of the past are over and thus the politics of the past need to be dropped. Which is fairly directly in contradiction of non-alternative-facts where many conditions of the past have yet to go away; thus the politics of them are not over either.<br /> <br /> Which is also kind of funny considering their official platform still engages in identity politics in places... so at least the rest of the Justice Democrats seem to recognize that Kyle's statements in that moment weren't on point. They specifically call for things that are not matters of universality; such as sexuality and gender based amendments to ensure their status as protected groups along with ethnicity, religion, and so on. There's a plank about fighting for women's rights. One of the planks has a more universality focused tone, but then calls out specific policies for their discriminatory nature. <br /> <br /> So yeah, the Justice Democrats as a whole might have their heads on their shoulders in this regard, even if Kyle discussed it poorly... and since I was talking about Kyle and your statement about how important his voice is, not their movement as a whole, I think my points still stand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's what it should be about yes. That doesn't mean Kyle or Sargon are good messengers for it, or that the Justice Democrats as a whole have a solid grasp on how to accomplish this.<br /> <br /> The self-sabotaging rhetoric is a problem for this goal. Bringing people together means... also bringing the wealthy and powerful together with the rest of us. Yes, we need to make sure they're helping not &amp;quot;leading&amp;quot; but rejecting them completely is not a form of bringing people together.<br /> <br /> The purity primary tactic is a problem for this goal. That's tossing people out rather than bringing them together.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> We're also still waiting for this evidence thing you were going to provide.</div> </div> </div> </div> The top goal is to get Money out of politics, still the rich can give their opinions and advice like anyone else, heck as a Canadian I don't think it's legal for me to give money, but that doesn't mean I can offer advise and moral support, just like a rich person can. <br /> <br /> It's not a personal attack on rich people to say they don't want they money, it's why would a rich person be bothered by it, it does them no harm, and if they support Justice Democracts, then they likely want big money out of politics too, so they would back this move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:56:25-08:00","id":1043825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043650#post1043650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words have meaning, the excuse people use to over react to everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so if people start a trend to redefine, &quot;MRA&quot; to mean, &quot;Macho Rapist Apologia.&quot; and enough people start using it that 75% or more of people think that's what it means, you're going to be cool with it?<br /> <br /> &quot;Over react&quot; the Internet version of, &quot;I'm not a bully, they're just a crybaby.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ACTIONS have meaning, words have inturpratations the are skewed by the listeners personality and beliefs. </div> </div> </div>And <b>labeling</b> people is an action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043670#post1043670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The top goal is to get Money out of politics, still the rich can give their opinions and advice like anyone else, heck as a Canadian I don't think it's legal for me to give money, but that doesn't mean I can offer advise and moral support, just like a rich person can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've addressed this a few times now. I don't see how my feelings on how the Justice Democrats (who do not cite this as their sole or first and foremost goal) actually go about this are not clear. Didn't you just make the &quot;actions&quot; not &quot;words&quot; argument? Doesn't that mean they need to <b>act</b> in ways that achieve these goals, not just use words that make it sound like they care about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not a personal attack on rich people to say they don't want they money, it's why would a rich person be bothered by it, it does them no harm, and if they support Justice Democracts, then they likely want big money out of politics too, so they would back this move. </div> </div> </div>It's insulting to the intelligence of everyone to say, &quot;We'll take your money if you're worth $900 million, because that's not the rich buying us, but $1 billion is over the line.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's an insult to the thousands of small businesses that are corporations to say that they're the same as giant multinational megacorps.<br /> <br /> Again, this is an issue with your refuse to acknowledge the reality of things on the ground here no matter how many times you're told (or go research it yourself). We don't need, &quot;No money from billionaires and corporations!&quot; because that's not the problem. We need transparency and loophole closing that lets the rich and powerful ignore the contribution limits that are supposed to keep them from buying politicians. We need pressure to not just overturn Citizens United, but to get the definition of 501c(4) enforced to stop letting political operatives use them as dark money machines; since that's way more important than SuperPACs to this goal (and not even on their list).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T00:04:05-08:00","id":1043878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1042572#post1042572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all well and good, but the traditional meaning of corporatism does not make it the same thing as neo-liberalism.<br /> <br /> Do you want politicians to support stronger vocational and trade unions, and similar collective citizen organizations as a counter to the power of the wealthy and corporations?<br /> <br /> That means in traditional poli-sci definitions, you're a corporatist. Corporatism in traditional terms is fuckthe beli ef that collective citizen organizations should have a strong place in politics. Progressives have traditionally embraced corporatism based values because it means empowering common citizens to for politically active citizen organizations to use numbers in a democracy to push against the power that collects in the hands of the wealthy.<br /> <br /> I hate it when people my gross and dismissive generalizations about things that can be shown to be false with a simple Google search. There's a lot of political conversations out there around spending and corporate power. Now, I can see a decent frustration about the lack of depth in many of these conversations, but they tend to get wonky very quickly which turns a lot of people off (and then doesn't get a lot of public attention).<br /> <br /> It's not true, but the impression has a valid source. The US political system was designed to pressure the government towards centrist/compromise policies. The whole idea was that no matter how far about the primary political blocs are in US politics, the system is meant to pull them together. This, of course, means that the results make them look &quot;samey&quot; because they're compromising to get laws passed in a system that assumes well deliberated laws that seek to use the best ideas of each political ideology at the table will in aggregate get the best laws.<br /> <br /> That intent isn't working out all that well right now, but that doesn't mean the parties are really the same with some minor differences. They're just working in the same system.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if unions have been better for the system and not worse. My issue is that there are very loose checks and balances on corporations. I can't believe I'm saying this but one of the few positives of this situation is the removal of the TPPA agreement. Which would have made corporations able to sue governments, which is ridiculous. The issue is a majority of republicans and democrats in power don't give a fuck they are in the pockets of big business or moving into those positions when they retired.<br /> <br /> That said I do agree with you over justices democrats. I don't think you can win without money but what really needs to be changed is lobbyists. Lobbyists are the issue that ruin parity.<br /> <br /> When I said it's superficial, it was disingenuous. I'm just upset over the current state of politics. Abortion, identity politics and immigration took the forefront of this election,these three things took 90% of the fucking election. When at most they should have been 30%. They are important but to dictate the flow of the entire election on these three things was bullshit. I mean when Bernie lost I just didn't vote. Partially because I moved and I wasn't going to influence the local policies of a place I'm not going to live in long term. Partially because neither presidential candidate represented my beliefs and I wasn't going to vote for someone because the other person was worse. That's not a vote. Also I live in a blue state so it didn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T21:50:22-08:00","id":1044373,"title":"","content":"It seemed like 90% was taken up by Hillary and Trump scandals, maybe it only seemed that way from Canada, but I guess those 3 things we're mixed in as part of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:25:21-08:00","id":1044384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1043825#post1043825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, so if people start a trend to redefine, &amp;quot;MRA&amp;quot; to mean, &amp;quot;Macho Rapist Apologia.&amp;quot; and enough people start using it that 75% or more of people think that's what it means, you're going to be cool with it?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Over react&amp;quot; the Internet version of, &amp;quot;I'm not a bully, they're just a crybaby.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And <b>labeling</b> people is an action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've addressed this a few times now. I don't see how my feelings on how the Justice Democrats (who do not cite this as their sole or first and foremost goal) actually go about this are not clear. Didn't you just make the &amp;quot;actions&amp;quot; not &amp;quot;words&amp;quot; argument? Doesn't that mean they need to <b>act</b> in ways that achieve these goals, not just use words that make it sound like they care about it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's insulting to the intelligence of everyone to say, &amp;quot;We'll take your money if you're worth $900 million, because that's not the rich buying us, but $1 billion is over the line.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It's an insult to the thousands of small businesses that are corporations to say that they're the same as giant multinational megacorps.<br /> <br /> Again, this is an issue with your refuse to acknowledge the reality of things on the ground here no matter how many times you're told (or go research it yourself). We don't need, &amp;quot;No money from billionaires and corporations!&amp;quot; because that's not the problem. We need transparency and loophole closing that lets the rich and powerful ignore the contribution limits that are supposed to keep them from buying politicians. We need pressure to not just overturn Citizens United, but to get the definition of 501c(4) enforced to stop letting political operatives use them as dark money machines; since that's way more important than SuperPACs to this goal (and not even on their list).</div> </div> </div> </div> I laughed at that MRA example, I have weird sense of humour. <br /> <br /> Look if calling certain Democracts Corporatists invovled some kind of Slander like your MRA example, then you'd have a point, but these people earned the title, they've taken millions in of dollars from Corporations that expected special treatment, don't kid yourself that money was not &quot;free&quot; there are strings attached. <br /> <br /> Donations from Corporations and Unions should be banned period, should be limited from individuals just like in Canada's federal elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T01:15:30-08:00","id":1044416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1044384#post1044384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look if calling certain Democracts Corporatists invovled some kind of Slander like your MRA example, then you'd have a point, but these people earned the title, they've taken millions in of dollars from Corporations that expected special treatment, don't kid yourself that money was not &quot;free&quot; there are strings attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite your normal hypocrisy about the MRM (a movement that has demonstrated repeatedly that no matter how many &quot;good&quot; members there are, the only thing they can achieve as a group is convincing men that it's the woman's fault he raped her), you have been given plenty of chances to demonstrate your libelous (even if not legally so, but this is writing, not speaking) claims about how all the non-Justice Democrats are corrupt and act out the whims of their corporate masters. You've yet to actually cite a single reputable source for your claims.<br /> <br /> Sure, money influences politicians. But the Democrats have passed or at least voted for (depending on the period in recent history) a lot of stuff that's does not demonstrate just being in the pockets of these supposed corporate masters you're claiming they all follow.<br /> <br /> And none of this actually addresses the stupidity of using a word that doesn't mean what people are using it for just because it sounds good as a slogan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Donations from Corporations and Unions should be banned period, should be limited from individuals just like in Canada's federal elections. </div> </div> </div>And again, you seem to lack the basics on this. You haven't even gone to fucking Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> Corporations and unions are banned from contributing to campaigns. They cannot donate to candidates (puts a bit of a damper in the whole &quot;they're all bought&quot; thing a bit doesn't it...).<br /> <br /> There is a cap on personal individual donations.<br /> <br /> Man, it's almost like the law here isn't some cesspool in every area.<br /> <br /> The problems are (1) PACs, and specifically SuperPACs and (2) 501(c)(4) groups.<br /> <br /> The SuperPAC issue is relatively new (the Courts were the problem here, the legislature didn't even have to change anything) starting in 2010. PACs increased in funding 10x what they used to because of rulings in the Courts, since the main kinds of PACs before hand had (get this!) donation caps! The other kinds of PACs are all linked to the candidate in some fashion, and because of that are still subject to those rules. The last kind of PAC is a fully independent PAC that does no coordinate with the candidate. And the Courts ruled that this last kind cannot be subjected to any financial limitations by the government on the grounds of free speech.<br /> <br /> 501(c)(4) groups add to this problem because unlike PACs (even SuperPACs) they don't have do disclose who their donors are. 501(c)(4) is a tax-exempt designation for &quot;social welfare&quot; organizations that are not inherently and/or solely charities (which is 501(c)(3)). The problem is that while 501(c)(4) and it's lack of a requirement to disclose donors is meant to be for organizations that are for social welfare, this has been abused to create organizations that are really political funds. 501(c)(4)s, because they can participate in politics on some level, only have to disclose how much money they give to campaigns. This is where all the dark money problems come in. If a donor just gives shit tons of money to a SuperPAC, everyone knows it. If a donor gives the same amount of money to lots of 501(c)(4)s that then give the money to SuperPACs, <b>there is no way to know how their money got donated</b>. <br /> <br /> The SuperPAC problem is something that we would need either a constitutional Amendment or a liberal shift in the SCOTUS to deal with (it was a 5-4 decision along ideological grounds).<br /> <br /> The 501(c)(4) issue shouldn't actually be an issue. The problem is, well, the IRS is in charge of reviewing 501(c) classifications, and nobody likes the IRS or considers them a regulatory body (they just take your money and audit you). The last few times the IRS tried to enforce the 501(c)(4) classifications as written by law, it turned into a political shitstorm as people tried to claim the IRS was interfering with politics. Keep in mind, there's plenty of other 501(c) tax-exempt options; they just require donor disclosures. The Republican House went as far as to initiate investigations into IRS bureaucrats for trying to enforce the laws as written (because there was a misconception that the were targeting conservative groups).<br /> <br /> All of the people using 501(c)(4)s to funnel vast sums of money to SuperPACs to allow virtually unlimited donations are actually breaking the law, but the government body responsible for enforcing that is constantly told not to do so because most people have no idea how any of this works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:44:02-08:00","id":1044731,"title":"","content":"I never said all none Justice Democracts are corrupt, it's a select group of politicians that are. <br /> <br /> And this thread isn't about the MRM, I don't want this thread to disappear like my MRA, thread so please let's move away from that angle, there is no link between the MRM and Justice Democracts, beyond some MRAs sending feedback to the Justice Democracts, so I refuse to take your baiting on that. <br /> <br /> Anyways an update from Kyle <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=0vPWcFtbT9g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=0vPWcFtbT9g</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-06-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:13:52-08:00","id":1044797,"title":"","content":"Since there was some discussion of the meaning of &quot;corporatist&quot; and &quot;corporatism&quot; I thought this article link would be pertinent. There are various meanings (which a quick Google search will show) and the context in which they are used is important in determining which definition is being used, if one wishes to have a productive discussion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.salon.com/2014/01/05/the_corporatist_confusion_why_a_prominent_political_term_needs_to_be_retired/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.salon.com/2014/01/05/the_...to_be_retired/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:17:44-08:00","id":1044798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1044731#post1044731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said all none Justice Democracts are corrupt, it's a select group of politicians that are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who then?<br /> <br /> Who needs to be &quot;purged&quot; from the Democratic party? That's something the Justice Democrats are saying needs to happen (because they're talking primary challenges), and something you're supporting.<br /> <br /> The only name floated so far is Cory Booker... which is absurd (esp. if you have Bob Menendez in you want to go after a NJ Democratic Senator, oh look, it took me zero time to point to a Democrat that needs to be out of office, but his trial is later this year anyway).<br /> <br /> You've said you had evidence. We've asked for specifics. You're still on... nada. Put up or just stand back because you keep showing you do not know enough to offer advice about this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:40:24-08:00","id":1044829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/26/1625661/-The-Justice-Democrats-The-Future-of-the-Democratic-Party\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.dailykos.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/images/242400/original/Young-Turks-Cenk-Uygur.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/26/1625661/-The-Justice-Democrats-The-Future-of-the-Democratic-Party\" target=\"_blank\"> The Justice Democrats: The Future of the Democratic Party </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/26/1625661/-The-Justice-Democrats-The-Future-of-the-Democratic-Party\" target=\"_blank\"> http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/26/1625661/-The-Justice-Democrats-The-Future-of-the-Democratic-Party </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Support Justice Democrats for a reformed, people-powered Democratic Party&mdash;discover their platform and join the movement now. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:48:58-08:00","id":1044835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;rct=j&amp;url=/amp/www.marketwatch.com/amp/story/guid/B9E50B50-7CB5-11E5-9449-5AB5D402F8F1&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiDotW6if3RAhWF5oMKHUPZCF8QFghHMAs&amp;usg=AFQjCNFhIyfEy7g_7cBlm_GhDH_bMCweNA&amp;sig2=9tmI-mSKalTwnYaGVz8evA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;rct=j&amp;url=/amp/www.marketwatch.com/amp/story/guid/B9E50B50-7CB5-11E5-9449-5AB5D402F8F1&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiDotW6if3RAhWF5oMKHUPZCF8QFghHMAs&amp;usg=AFQjCNFhIyfEy7g_7cBlm_GhDH_bMCweNA&amp;sig2=9tmI-mSKalTwnYaGVz8evA\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;rct=j&amp;url=/amp/www.marketwatch.com/amp/story/guid/B9E50B50-7CB5-11E5-9449-5AB5D402F8F1&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiDotW6if3RAhWF5oMKHUPZCF8QFghHMAs&amp;usg=AFQjCNFhIyfEy7g_7cBlm_GhDH_bMCweNA&amp;sig2=9tmI-mSKalTwnYaGVz8evA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;rct=j&amp;url=/amp/www.marketwatch.com/amp/story/guid/B9E50B50-7CB5-11E5-9449-5AB5D402F8F1&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiDotW6if3RAhWF5oMKHUPZCF8QFghHMAs&amp;usg=AFQjCNFhIyfEy7g_7cBlm_GhDH_bMCweNA&amp;sig2=9tmI-mSKalTwnYaGVz8evA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll have more later stuff later, but on my time table, not yours, I have to deal with work today, I have an ice storm hitting today!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:49:32-08:00","id":1044836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1044797#post1044797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there was some discussion of the meaning of &amp;quot;corporatist&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;corporatism&amp;quot; I thought this article link would be pertinent. There are various meanings (which a quick Google search will show) and the context in which they are used is important in determining which definition is being used, if one wishes to have a productive discussion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://www.salon.com/2014/01/05/the_corporatist_confusion_why_a_prominent_political_term_needs_to_be_retired/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.salon.com/2014/01/05/the_...to_be_retired/</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T20:38:33-08:00","id":1044861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1044829#post1044829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/26/1625661/-The-Justice-Democrats-The-Future-of-the-Democratic-Party\" target=\"_blank\">http://m.dailykos.com/story/2017/1/2...mocratic-Party</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So... a DKos poster just saying corporate money is corrupting. No specifics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1044835#post1044835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;rct=j&amp;url=/amp/www.marketwatch.com/amp/story/guid/B9E50B50-7CB5-11E5-9449-5AB5D402F8F1&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiDotW6if3RAhWF5oMKHUPZCF8QFghHMAs&amp;usg=AFQjCNFhIyfEy7g_7cBlm_GhDH_bMCweNA&amp;sig2=9tmI-mSKalTwnYaGVz8evA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.ca/url?sa=t&amp;sourc...alTwnYaGVz8evA</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And... just a chart of donations with no link to which candidates they gave to, and how those candidates voted.<br /> <br /> If you're going to be back with more, can it be something substantive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:32:20-08:00","id":1048280,"title":"","content":"The coalition's been founded by someone who's a co-founded of a news channel named after a group that took part in the Armenian Genocide, which is still being denied to this day.<br /> <br /> That's not a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:13:40-08:00","id":1048328,"title":"","content":"However unfortunate it is, &quot;Young Turk&quot; in American politics refers to the start of the Young Turks (as a contrast to the American Revolutionary figures who were largely older established land owners vs. a monarch) and ignores the horrible things the CUP did after gaining power (though... we do tend to overlook what the Founding Fathers and the next generation of US leadership did as well... so it's a cowardly consistent comparison).<br /> <br /> While Cenk himself (as noted up-thread) was an Armenian Genocide denier, he's backed off that stance. I think he's handled it poorly, but his turn around does seem to coincide with his political about face as well. I'm willing to give the man some credit as a Turkish immigrant to the US, who seemed to embrace extremely conservative politics until the Bush era, then started to question his political beliefs and re-examine them; eventually at least leading to recant is denials. Not a lot of credit mind you, but it's better than you'll get out of a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Also while he has had troubles with his handling of the Armenian Genocide, and the TYT founders in general didn't really handle their naming choice that well, the actual content the TYT has put out has largely avoided controversy in this particular area (it probably didn't hurt that they eventually hired an Armenian American journalist to their team to at least content check against it, since I haven't seen any attempts to just use her as a shield against criticism over the name).<br /> <br /> So, I don't think it's fair to put too much on the Justice Democrats for Cenk's choices previously. It's not a good thing, but I don't think it's a disqualifying thing either. I'd rather give people some pass for changing their views towards a less problematic view of history, than never let them live it down if they've done nothing since their change to doubt it's sincerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:10:17-08:00","id":1048753,"title":"","content":"Cenk had a bit to say on this podcast. Honestly, I found his inflammatory rhetoric kind of alarming. Whatever his roots or choice of terms might be, I don't think he'll be persuasive to anyone <i>other </i>than those clamoring for revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/player/embed/515059913/515060837\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.npr.org/include/images/facebook-default-wide-s1400-c100.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/player/embed/515059913/515060837\" target=\"_blank\"> The Blueprint: What's Next For Democrats? : 1A </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/player/embed/515059913/515060837\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.npr.org/player/embed/515059913/515060837 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Democratic party is out of power in Washington and in two-thirds of state legislatures. Even with the country's changing demographics on its side, the party is more removed from power than it has been at almost any point before. The same voters who had previously embraced the New Deal, built the Great Society and put their hope in the nation's first black president are not turning up in the numbers they once did. The party has been described as being on life support. What will it take to bring it back to health? Guests include Cenk Uygur, co-host of \"The Young Turks\", Rep. Cheri Bustos (D-Illinois, 17th District), Stacey Abrams, House Minority Leader for the Georgia General Assembly and State Representative for the 89th House District, Symone Sanders, political strategist, Margie Omero, Democratic strategist and pollster, and Rich Benjamin, senior fellow at Demos. </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> I don't want revolution. I want <i>reformation. </i>There is an important difference there. I find myself more on board with Simone Sanders in this discussion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-14-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:51:31-08:00","id":1048824,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was not really a great way to convince any of us that look at his &quot;rhetoric more than substance,&quot; approach that he'll need to do if he thinks 100,000 national progressives is enough alone to primary anyone.<br /> <br /> The &quot;get rid of them all&quot; attitude isn't going to work, even if he has any good points to make. It's also kinda of depressing to see him jump on the whole &quot;alternative facts&quot; bandwagon has he rails against corporate money in politics, while name checking FDR and LBJ... who were completely in bed with various corporate powers. It might be strange, but US political history shows (repeatedly) that progressives can fight for progressive policies and still have corporate donors (and frankly, neither FDR or LBJ were particularly strong progressives in a modern sense, and having more centrist appeal was a huge factor for both getting the progressive stuff that they did done).<br /> <br /> Slogans over substance might make win some elections in the short term, but isn't not something that's going to sell well to people that want a government that actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:12:00-08:00","id":1049378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1040292-justice-democracy-s-very-excited?p=1048280#post1048280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The coalition's been founded by someone who's a co-founded of a news channel named after a group that took part in the Armenian Genocide, which is still being denied to this day.<br /> <br /> That's not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're just big Rod Stewart fans...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:29:52-08:00","id":1051146,"title":"","content":"Cenk is always been bombastic, but the TYT has a massive audience, and Secular Talk has a sizable audience as well, plus there are key members of Bernie Sanders team, so 100,000 members are just a beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:39:01-08:00","id":1051241,"title":"","content":"Cenk being bombastic isn't a good thing for long term success.<br /> <br /> TYT having a massive audience (though compared to what?) means nothing. An audience isn't a political movement.<br /> <br /> The key members of Sanders' team means... what? They couldn't mobilize enough to beat Clinton, and they couldn't mobilize enough to get progressive populists traction in down-ballot races either. Besides proving that they can raise a lot of money from the grassroots, what do they have a proven track record of actually doing on getting people elected or getting policies passed?<br /> <br /> And 100,000 isn't a beginning. It's a burp. You need ~50K voters to come out to win a primary on an off year in a small non-competitive not-high turn out Congressional district. And all of them need to be registered voters in one place. There's 435 districts to worry about. And 34 Senate elections which are mostly in states with a lot more primary voters than that. And this isn't something that they can grow in a few years. The next mid-term elections are in less than two years, which means mobilization needs to start in less than a year at a minimum.<br /> <br /> The Indivisible movement is already making the Social Democrats look like chumps. Their numbers are hard to know exactly, but they already have 6,000 local groups spread in almost every State, and greater public support than the Tea Party ever had. And they're doing it without &quot;bombastic&quot; self-sabotage purity threats. Instead of whining about corporate money, they're actually being the progressive grassroots and trying to turn the progressive anger about the election and first month of the administration into a movement that will change the face of elections to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T09:09:52-08:00","id":1051540,"title":"","content":"Indivisible groups are interesting, but they are no substititute for Justice Democracts, the Indivisbles are focused on Trump, which is fine, the Justice Democracts focused on fixing the Democracts so they can take on Trump and know what to do once they get there. Indivisible is just a guide on how to deal with your local Congressmen. It has it's use, don't get me wrong, but it's no replacement for the vital work being done by Justice Democracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:07:58-08:00","id":1051659,"title":"","content":"Yet again, you're not showing any actual knowledge of what's going on here (also, how's the examples of Democrats who have caved to corporate donors over their stated ideology going? Still waiting on you to come up with something).<br /> <br /> Indivisible groups are doing a lot more than protesting Trump. They're also organizing grass root activism to go after both Republican and Democratic politicians to ensure that the left's voice isn't ignored in a time of the right having so much control. Which is what we actually need the public to be doing: making it clear that a voter backlash is coming and they all need to realize which side of the line they want to be one when it comes.<br /> <br /> And what is this &quot;vital work&quot; that the Justice Democrats are actually doing? As far as I can tell it's just a bunch of pundits and high end political operatives trying to take control of the party to run things their way; which isn't working because most people on the left don't like their way. The US left is - generally speaking - happy that our versions of Rush Limbaugh, Glenn Beck (sorta, he's actually gotten a bit better since he's realized how bad the hyper-conservative media thing turned out to be for his own beliefs), Alex Jones, and so on are not house hold names because they don't have major sway on politics. We don't want to fall into the pit the Republican's have fallen into of letting the most bombastic purity focused personalities constantly drag things further and further to the left until logic, reason, and policy all stop mattering in the name of ideological purity. Which is, as far as I can tell, all the Justice Democrats are really working towards accomplishing; whatever they say their goals are.<br /> <br /> If Cenk wants to be the new Rush, fuck Cenk, If you actually care about the health of the progressive movement in my country, how about you do more listening and research before you think you know enough to give &quot;advice?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T17:01:29-08:00","id":1051752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/amp.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/10/obama-donors-top-embassy-jobs-rewards?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/amp.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/10/obama-donors-top-embassy-jobs-rewards?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/s/amp.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/10/obama-donors-top-embassy-jobs-rewards?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.ca/amp/s/amp.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/10/obama-donors-top-embassy-jobs-rewards?client=ms-android-bell-ca </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/m.huffpost.com/us/entry/us_579927d5e4b0d3568f85d91a/amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_co